    "created_at": "2018-06-01T21:58:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-06-01T21:58:05Z",
    "body": "No, but I don't like breaking things for the sake of breaking things. \r\n\r\nIf you want to set \"visibility:hidden\" on an element, you can absolutely set \"visibility:hidden\" on it. I understand the value of using visibility:collapse for table rows and table columns, as visibility:collapse is some sort of smart display:none, and I think a breaking change there is acceptable for these. But for table-cells, I don't see a strong reason to behave differently as to, say, a grid. \r\n\r\nIn the http archive you came up with at least one case where this would matter, so I would want more than just a 50%-50% poll to justify a breaking change in all browsers.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
